WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.759
Everything you've ever touched is built from a short list of particles.

2
00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.902
Let's meet them.

3
00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:15.644
This is the Standard Model: every known building block of matter, and the forces that act on them.

4
00:00:16.044 --> 00:00:22.482
Quarks in pink, leptons in green, force carriers in orange, and the Higgs boson in gold.

5
00:00:23.282 --> 00:00:29.961
Up and down quarks live inside protons and neutrons, constantly trading colour charge through gluons.

6
00:00:30.762 --> 00:00:36.145
Flip to antimatter, and every particle gets a mirror twin with the opposite charge.

7
00:00:36.945 --> 00:00:44.924
The top quark is the heaviest of all, as heavy as a gold atom. It decays in less than a trillionth of a trillionth of a second.

8
00:00:45.724 --> 00:00:54.561
When an electron meets its antimatter twin, both vanish in two flashes of gamma rays. Hospitals use this in PET scans.

9
00:00:55.361 --> 00:01:03.183
Muons rain down from cosmic rays. They should decay long before reaching the ground, but relativity slows their clocks.

10
00:01:03.983 --> 00:01:10.420
Neutrinos are ghostly. Trillions pass through you every second, and they change flavour as they travel.

11
00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:17.631
Gluons carry colour themselves, so they cling together into tubes, which snap rather than stretch forever.

12
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:24.689
Photons are ripples of light. When one hits an atom, it can kick an electron up to a higher level.

13
00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:31.618
The W boson turns one kind of quark into another. That's how radioactive decay works.

14
00:01:32.418 --> 00:01:38.274
And the Higgs field fills all of space. The more a particle drags on it, the more mass it has.

15
00:01:38.873 --> 00:01:44.106
When a Higgs boson decays into two Z bosons, their spins are quantum entangled.

16
00:01:45.906 --> 00:01:51.341
One particle is still missing: the graviton, the carrier of gravity, never yet seen.

17
00:01:54.866 --> 00:01:57.212
Twelve matter particles build everything.

18
00:01:57.312 --> 00:01:59.606
Forces are carried by particles too.

19
00:01:59.705 --> 00:02:01.593
And mass comes from the Higgs field.

20
00:02:02.266 --> 00:02:04.337
Next time: the four forces.
